    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist for Multi-Node Language-Model Serving Systems\n\n## Purpose and Scope\n\nThis checklist validates that a distributed LLM serving system (tensor-parallel, pipeline-parallel, expert-parallel, or data-parallel deployments) behaves correctly under realistic conditions. It is designed to catch silent failures \u2014 the most dangerous class of bugs in distributed systems, where a node drops out or misbehaves but the system continues returning plausible-looking output.\n\n**Ground rule:** Every check below must produce a *recorded artifact* (log line, metric snapshot, file hash, or signed report). A check that cannot produce evidence has not been performed.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\n**Goal:** Prove that every node in the cluster is running the exact same logical configuration, and that the configuration you validated is the configuration in production.\n\n### 1.1 Static configuration fingerprinting\n\n- [ ] Compute a canonical hash (e.g., SHA-256 over a normalized serialization \u2014 sorted keys, no timestamps, no hostnames) of the full serving configuration on **every node independently**.\n- [ ] Verify all hashes match. Do not rely on \"the config was pushed from one place\" \u2014 verify the *received* bytes on each node.\n- [ ] Include in the fingerprint: model path/URI, model revision (git SHA or content hash, **not** a mutable tag like `main` or `latest`), tokenizer files, quantization settings, parallelism degrees (TP/PP/EP/DP), max sequence length, KV-cache size, sampling defaults, and scheduler parameters.\n- [ ] Verify the model weights hash matches across all nodes that hold shards. For sharded models, hash each shard and record the shard-to-rank mapping.\n- [ ] Confirm the tokenizer is byte-identical across nodes (a tokenizer mismatch produces subtly wrong output with no error).\n- [ ] Record versions of: inference engine, CUDA/ROCm, driver, NCCL/",
      "reasoning": "",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
